Which that I shall not do for love or money.
My mistress' eyes are nothing like the sun;
If I could write the beauty of your eyes,
And in my blood there runs a madness so;
Unto the green velvet of the new-born leaves;
And keep my thoughts to myself, to see,
The living record of your memory.
But that black mould is dead to us, and gone;
